course: dictionary
lesson: 2793
title: Dispatch: sending and speed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one to use. «The online shop will dispatch your parcel today.» Here dispatch means send, because a parcel is being sent to you.
explain: Dispatch can also be a noun, meaning an official message or a news report sent from far away. «The reporter sent a dispatch from the far-away island.» The reporter sent a message, so dispatch is the report itself.
explain: Use the swap check. Put "send" into the sentence: «The call centre sent an ambulance to the house» still makes sense, so dispatched means sent to do a job. Try the same check every time you meet a word with more than one meaning.
explain: Dispatched can also mean killed quickly, as in «A hunter dispatched the animal quickly.» This meaning is formal or old-fashioned, so you will meet it less often than the meaning send.
fact: Dispatch is a verb and a noun: you can dispatch a parcel, or read a dispatch.
fact: «Dispatch» means to send something or someone to a place, such as a parcel, a letter or an ambulance.
fact: «With dispatch» means quickly and efficiently, so «She finished the homework with dispatch» means she finished it fast.
fact: Emergency call centres dispatch ambulances, fire engines and police to people who need help.
fact: In maths, dispatched items leave a warehouse, so the stock in the warehouse goes down.
exercise: «The online shop will dispatch your parcel on Monday.» What does dispatch mean here? | *Send off | Keep safe for a long time | Open carefully | Wrap in paper
exercise: «The reporter sent a dispatch from the far-away island.» What is a dispatch here? | A ship that carries people | *An official message or news report sent from far away | A type of bird | A small, hot drink
exercise: «The call centre dispatched an ambulance to the house.» What does dispatched mean? | Cooked for dinner | *Sent to do a job | Hidden under a bed | Painted bright blue
test: «She finished the homework with dispatch.» What does with dispatch mean? | *Quickly and efficiently | Slowly and carefully | Without any help | Angrily
test: A new word appears in a text and has more than one meaning. What is a good way to check which meaning fits? | Ask someone who is not at school | Skip it and never come back to it | *Swap in a possible meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense | Count the letters in the word
exam: The warehouse dispatches 200 items a day, so the stock goes down. What does dispatches mean here? | *Sends out | Breaks | Buys in | Counts up
